{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1461680633,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNTExNDg3NzM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/417","origin":"github"},"title":"Development direction wrt to SSH usage","message":"We use SSH in a few places and we need SSH's controlmaster feature. Currently, SSH is treated as god-given shell binary. My question is: what is our general development direction in this regard.\n1. Ignore. Currently implementation is unlikely to work on Windows (Mac OS I am not sure either) and we are OK with that.\n2. Acknowledge partially and ignore for now. We create a minimall SSH wrapper class that we use in our code base to secure a better chance to support SSH better in the future with justifiable effort.\n3. Switch to using a proper Wrapper like http://www.paramiko.org or https://github.com/mwilliamson/spur.py (both in Debian) hoping that they bring some improvement in cross platform support.","files":null}]}